WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.271
A parent hands a navigator a stack of

2
00:00:02.271 --> 00:00:04.292
papers and says, I don't know what any

3
00:00:04.292 --> 00:00:05.050
of this is.

4
00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:06.060
Where do you start?

5
00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:08.810
Not with all of it, I hope.

6
00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:09.720
Right.

7
00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:12.015
Find the one paper that matters now, explain

8
00:00:12.015 --> 00:00:13.770
it and write down the next step.

9
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.209
The whole path has five parts: first contact,

10
00:00:17.209 --> 00:00:20.418
assessment, planning and choice, services starting, and renewals

11
00:00:20.418 --> 00:00:21.220
and changes.

12
00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:24.257
But a family only needs the next step

13
00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:24.570
today.

14
00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:26.820
Who does the assessment in Minnesota?

15
00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:31.478
Lead agencies: counties, tribal nations and managed care

16
00:00:31.478 --> 00:00:35.346
organizations, using the state's MnCHOICES system and certified

17
00:00:35.346 --> 00:00:35.830
assessors.

18
00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:37.580
A navigator doesn't assess.

19
00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:39.970
A navigator helps the family get ready.

20
00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:42.829
Some families want to show they're doing fine,

21
00:00:42.829 --> 00:00:44.440
so nobody thinks they can't cope.

22
00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:45.870
That's very human.

23
00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:48.604
The navigator can explain that the assessment is

24
00:00:48.604 --> 00:00:50.888
how the agency learns what help might make

25
00:00:50.888 --> 00:00:53.172
life easier, and talk through a real week

26
00:00:53.172 --> 00:00:54.600
with them, hard nights included.

27
00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:57.648
Then the family decides what to share, in

28
00:00:57.648 --> 00:00:58.630
their own words.

29
00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:00.860
Preparing, never scripting.

30
00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:03.886
Then they get a list of providers and

31
00:01:03.886 --> 00:01:04.450
a deadline.

32
00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:06.440
And this is where the law helps.

33
00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:10.093
For people on waivers, Minnesota's informed decision-making process

34
00:01:10.093 --> 00:01:13.316
includes things like all available options, cultural needs,

35
00:01:13.316 --> 00:01:16.539
visits or hands-on experiences, talking with peers and

36
00:01:16.539 --> 00:01:18.150
enough time to decide.

37
00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:20.190
A family who knows they can ask for

38
00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:21.920
a visit is in a much stronger position.

39
00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:25.410
And once services are approved, it's done?

40
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:26.480
Not quite.

41
00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:28.650
That's when things quietly stall.

42
00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:31.188
Help the family know what should happen next,

43
00:01:31.188 --> 00:01:33.355
follow up with the case manager when they

44
00:01:33.355 --> 00:01:35.523
agree, read every letter together for dates and

45
00:01:35.523 --> 00:01:37.420
appeal rights, and keep a simple record.

46
00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:39.790
And free help along the way?

47
00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:43.360
Disability Hub MN is a free statewide resource.

48
00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:46.754
For health coverage, MNsure navigators help for free

49
00:01:46.754 --> 00:01:47.130
too.

50
00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:49.500
A navigator doesn't have to know everything.

51
00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:51.070
They have to know where to go.
